1
00:00:04,833 --> 00:00:11,800
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:32,633
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:34,933
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:41,033
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:43,867
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:43,867 --> 00:00:45,133
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,133 --> 00:00:46,800
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:48,533
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:51,033
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,367 --> 00:00:53,700
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:55,300
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,533 --> 00:00:57,967
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:57,967 --> 00:01:00,100
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:00,933 --> 00:01:03,067
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,133 --> 00:01:06,267
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,167 --> 00:01:09,200
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,033 --> 00:01:11,733
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,733 --> 00:01:12,900
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:14,233
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,933 --> 00:01:22,367
<i>Hey, Diday!
You're with someone beautiful.</i>

21
00:01:22,367 --> 00:01:24,800
She's my partner in doing nails.
<i> She's good.</i>

22
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:25,733
<i> Quit moving around, sir.</i>

23
00:01:25,867 --> 00:01:27,967
- You don't have to pay anymore.
<i> - Thank you!</i>

24
00:01:28,467 --> 00:01:29,967
<i> It smells like a burning--</i>

25
00:01:32,367 --> 00:01:33,333
<i> Sorry!</i>

26
00:01:33,333 --> 00:01:36,000
<i> If we win, we'll be loaded.</i>

27
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:37,167
<i>Do you know anything
about cockfighting?</i>

28
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:39,333
<i> Not at all.</i>

29
00:01:39,333 --> 00:01:41,733
<i>Come on, let's join them
and make a bet.</i>

30
00:01:41,767 --> 00:01:43,333
<i>- How's the team doing?
- We lost someone.</i>

31
00:01:43,333 --> 00:01:45,033
<i>- But we're still a team.
- What about the spy?</i>

32
00:01:45,033 --> 00:01:47,167
<i> The members of Team Alpha...</i>

33
00:01:47,167 --> 00:01:48,667
<i> You shouldn't trust--</i>

34
00:01:48,667 --> 00:01:52,033
<i>Pia, there is no spy
within Team Alpha.</i>

35
00:01:52,033 --> 00:01:55,067
<i>And if there is,
I'll keep my eyes open.</i>

36
00:01:55,067 --> 00:01:58,867
<i>I'll focus now
on the actual cases in NCIA,</i>

37
00:01:58,867 --> 00:02:01,400
<i> especially the case Sam left.</i>

38
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:02,633
<i> The one on Victor Zafra.</i>

39
00:02:02,633 --> 00:02:04,633
<i>They look like the ones
who are taking kidneys.</i>

40
00:02:04,633 --> 00:02:05,667
<i> Call Gabo.</i>

41
00:02:05,667 --> 00:02:07,633
<i>Gabo! Your enemies
from last night came back!</i>

42
00:02:07,633 --> 00:02:08,633
<i> What?</i>

43
00:02:10,233 --> 00:02:15,000
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

44
00:02:15,567 --> 00:02:17,000
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

45
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:18,400
Thank you.

46
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:21,567
The files in front of you

47
00:02:21,567 --> 00:02:24,300
are everything we have
on the Victor Zafra case.

48
00:02:24,733 --> 00:02:26,433
The last case
Ma'am Sam handled.

49
00:02:26,433 --> 00:02:28,367
We're no longer
merely seeking justice.

50
00:02:28,367 --> 00:02:30,900
Now, we're the ones
actively working for it.

51
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:34,367
We'll hold Victor Zafra
accountable for all his crimes.

52
00:02:34,367 --> 00:02:36,033
How about the whole Zafra clan?

53
00:02:36,533 --> 00:02:39,467
I still believe
they're the ones who killed Sam.

54
00:02:39,467 --> 00:02:41,867
If we could only make
Victor Zafra talk

55
00:02:41,867 --> 00:02:44,000
and tell us
everything he knows,

56
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:45,567
this would all be over.

57
00:02:45,567 --> 00:02:49,367
I'm sure
that's next to impossible.

58
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:50,633
But what we can do...

59
00:02:51,033 --> 00:02:52,733
is make other people
talk for him.

60
00:02:53,367 --> 00:02:54,300
Like who?

61
00:02:54,733 --> 00:02:56,200
How about that...

62
00:02:56,733 --> 00:02:57,733
long-haired guy?

63
00:02:57,733 --> 00:02:58,833
[SEBASTIAN] Mm.

64
00:02:58,833 --> 00:03:01,167
Isn't he one of Sam's
persons of interest?

65
00:03:01,967 --> 00:03:03,067
You're right.

66
00:03:03,867 --> 00:03:05,033
This guy...

67
00:03:06,533 --> 00:03:08,833
He knows a lot
about the Zafras.

68
00:03:09,333 --> 00:03:12,767
He probably knows something
about Sam's death, too.

69
00:03:12,767 --> 00:03:14,733
He might have even
been there that night.

70
00:03:16,667 --> 00:03:18,333
We need to find him.

71
00:03:19,033 --> 00:03:22,500
He's the key to holding
the Zafras accountable.

72
00:03:23,600 --> 00:03:25,567
And if he's
in any way involved...

73
00:03:28,133 --> 00:03:29,633
we'll make him pay, too.

74
00:03:33,233 --> 00:03:34,367
Are these all the videos?

75
00:03:34,367 --> 00:03:35,767
Yes, sir. That's all of it.

76
00:03:38,100 --> 00:03:39,133
Get a copy of these.

77
00:03:39,133 --> 00:03:42,600
And get the CCTV footage
at Ginintuang Lupa.

78
00:03:42,600 --> 00:03:45,200
Once you've done that,
delete everything.

79
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:47,367
Make sure
you don't leave a trace.

80
00:03:47,367 --> 00:03:48,500
Do you understand?

81
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:52,400
No one should know
we got a long-haired suspect.

82
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:55,433
If we find this man,
we'd get the gold back.

83
00:03:56,167 --> 00:03:57,633
Go on. Get it.

84
00:03:57,633 --> 00:04:04,500
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

85
00:04:06,433 --> 00:04:07,267
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS]

86
00:04:17,233 --> 00:04:20,067
Sir, make sure
we won't get busted for this.

87
00:04:22,033 --> 00:04:25,400
Then, make sure
no one else finds out.

88
00:04:25,400 --> 00:04:28,267
Because if we find
that long-haired guy,

89
00:04:28,300 --> 00:04:30,267
we'd take the gold back.

90
00:04:31,033 --> 00:04:33,767
And we'd keep that gold
all to ourselves.

91
00:04:33,767 --> 00:04:35,900
Every single one of them.

92
00:04:36,433 --> 00:04:39,833
We won't have to work
for another day in our lives.

93
00:04:40,200 --> 00:04:42,233
Because we'll be
drowning in money.

94
00:04:42,233 --> 00:04:43,800
Do you understand, Santos?

95
00:04:45,767 --> 00:04:46,767
Yes, sir.

96
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,067
Now, delete it.

97
00:04:56,733 --> 00:04:58,067
[COMPUTER TRILLS]

98
00:04:59,667 --> 00:05:01,033
They're all gone, sir.

99
00:05:02,133 --> 00:05:03,767
That's what I'm talking about.

100
00:05:03,767 --> 00:05:05,233
[CHUCKLES]

101
00:05:08,167 --> 00:05:09,533
[SANTOS] Smart plan, sir.

102
00:05:11,333 --> 00:05:12,633
Come in!

103
00:05:12,633 --> 00:05:13,700
Sir.

104
00:05:13,700 --> 00:05:15,133
- Sir.
- Yes?

105
00:05:15,133 --> 00:05:18,467
Any updates on the
safe house gold heist?

106
00:05:18,867 --> 00:05:20,000
[CLEARS THROAT]

107
00:05:22,167 --> 00:05:24,667
Uh, sir, we're already
working on it.

108
00:05:25,500 --> 00:05:28,633
And we asked around the area
to look for eyewitnesses.

109
00:05:28,633 --> 00:05:29,600
There's really none.

110
00:05:29,600 --> 00:05:31,300
How about the CCTV
in the safe house

111
00:05:31,300 --> 00:05:32,700
and surrounding areas?

112
00:05:32,700 --> 00:05:33,767
You got nothing too?

113
00:05:35,700 --> 00:05:38,067
We reviewed
all the CCTV footage, sir,

114
00:05:38,067 --> 00:05:40,400
but we didn't find
any new leads.

115
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:41,567
[DOMINGO SIGHS]

116
00:05:41,567 --> 00:05:42,600
Sir,

117
00:05:43,333 --> 00:05:46,333
I think it's just either
the Zafras

118
00:05:46,333 --> 00:05:47,733
or someone
from Ginintuang Lupa.

119
00:05:47,733 --> 00:05:49,600
Just what I previously
suspected.

120
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:50,967
Do you remember

121
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:54,500
our convoy that got ambushed

122
00:05:54,500 --> 00:05:58,067
while we're transferring
the gold to the safe house?

123
00:05:58,067 --> 00:06:00,900
My hunch was those thugs from
Ginintuang Lupa did that too.

124
00:06:00,900 --> 00:06:02,767
So how do you plan to proceed?

125
00:06:02,767 --> 00:06:03,833
Sir,

126
00:06:04,800 --> 00:06:07,200
we'll search
the whole Ginintuang Lupa.

127
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:10,033
We'll take out
all the traitors one by one.

128
00:06:10,067 --> 00:06:12,033
That's my plan
for retrieving the gold.

129
00:06:12,033 --> 00:06:15,067
Just make sure we get
those gold bars back.

130
00:06:15,067 --> 00:06:18,100
I don't want General Jacinto
saying we're incompetent again.

131
00:06:18,100 --> 00:06:19,467
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

132
00:06:19,467 --> 00:06:20,467
Okay.

133
00:06:25,100 --> 00:06:26,400
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [KNIFE SWISHING]

134
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:28,433
- Come on! Let's go there!
- Come on!

135
00:06:28,433 --> 00:06:30,133
- Hurry! Hurry! Follow him!
- Gabo!

136
00:06:30,133 --> 00:06:32,067
Gabo, he's not done
cutting my hair!

137
00:06:35,733 --> 00:06:37,600
- Man, wait for me!
- Okay!

138
00:06:37,600 --> 00:06:38,533
I'll be back!

139
00:06:42,867 --> 00:06:49,800
- [CROWD CLAMORING]
- [BLOWS LANDING]

140
00:06:53,067 --> 00:06:54,767
- Move!
- They're beating them up!

141
00:06:57,833 --> 00:06:59,500
- [KICK LANDS]
- [THWACKS]

142
00:06:59,500 --> 00:07:00,767
You jerks
really have the guts, huh?

143
00:07:01,567 --> 00:07:02,933
You had the nerve to come back!

144
00:07:04,300 --> 00:07:06,733
Now you won't
come out here alive!

145
00:07:07,933 --> 00:07:09,033
[KNIFE SWISHING]

146
00:07:09,033 --> 00:07:10,500
- [GUNSHOT]
- Argh!

147
00:07:10,500 --> 00:07:12,033
- [GUN THUDS]
- [GUNSHOTS]

148
00:07:12,033 --> 00:07:14,300
- [METALLIC SCHWING]
- [MAN GRUNTS] Argh!

149
00:07:14,300 --> 00:07:17,100
[GUNSHOTS]

150
00:07:17,133 --> 00:07:19,700
[PEOPLE SCREAMING]

151
00:07:19,700 --> 00:07:21,600
[SLINGSHOT STRETCHES, SNAPS]

152
00:07:22,767 --> 00:07:28,233
[GUNSHOTS CONTINUE]

153
00:07:29,467 --> 00:07:31,000
[SLINGSHOT SNAPS]

154
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:33,600
- [THWACKS]
- [DEBRIS FALLING]

155
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:36,100
[MEN GRUNTING]

156
00:07:37,800 --> 00:07:39,267
Let's disperse!

157
00:07:41,567 --> 00:07:43,233
- [GUNSHOTS]
- Chase them!

158
00:07:43,233 --> 00:07:45,167
[GUNSHOTS CONTINUE]

159
00:07:46,500 --> 00:07:48,300
[SLINGSHOT SNAPPING]

160
00:07:51,100 --> 00:07:57,867
[SOFT, DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

161
00:07:58,533 --> 00:07:59,500
Borromeo.

162
00:08:00,600 --> 00:08:01,600
Yes, ma'am?

163
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:04,100
How's your investigation going?

164
00:08:05,333 --> 00:08:07,033
Have you found out who...

165
00:08:07,733 --> 00:08:09,400
[WHISPERS] the mole is?

166
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:10,467
Not yet, ma'am.

167
00:08:11,133 --> 00:08:12,700
But if it's true

168
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:16,033
that there's a mole here
working for the Zafras,

169
00:08:16,033 --> 00:08:17,400
it sure isn't on Team Alpha.

170
00:08:18,633 --> 00:08:21,400
So that's it, huh?

171
00:08:21,433 --> 00:08:24,733
We'll just accept that Jacinto

172
00:08:24,733 --> 00:08:27,333
was just another victim
of the Zafras?

173
00:08:28,567 --> 00:08:31,167
And there's nothing we can do?

174
00:08:32,300 --> 00:08:35,867
Ma'am, the whole team
is doing their best

175
00:08:35,867 --> 00:08:39,000
to hold the Zafras accountable
for killing Sam.

176
00:08:40,033 --> 00:08:44,333
And based on my observation,

177
00:08:44,333 --> 00:08:46,800
the team is working hard
to capture the Zafras.

178
00:08:46,800 --> 00:08:47,833
Is that so?

179
00:08:48,967 --> 00:08:51,667
Keep me posted, alright?

180
00:08:52,933 --> 00:08:54,433
Yes, ma'am.

181
00:08:54,467 --> 00:08:55,867
And don't worry,

182
00:08:55,867 --> 00:08:59,233
that family of criminals
will soon be reunited

183
00:08:59,233 --> 00:09:00,300
in jail.

184
00:09:02,367 --> 00:09:03,367
I'll get going, ma'am.

185
00:09:05,033 --> 00:09:11,967
[SOFT, DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

186
00:09:29,733 --> 00:09:31,733
- [PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [DOOR OPENS]

187
00:09:31,733 --> 00:09:32,700
Sir?

188
00:09:33,567 --> 00:09:34,500
Yes?

189
00:09:35,100 --> 00:09:36,067
Come in.

190
00:09:37,567 --> 00:09:38,567
[DOOR CLOSES]

191
00:09:38,567 --> 00:09:40,133
- [DELGADO] Yes?
- Uh...

192
00:09:40,133 --> 00:09:41,267
Can I talk to you, sir?

193
00:09:42,333 --> 00:09:43,567
About what, Sebastian?

194
00:09:48,100 --> 00:09:50,933
It's about getting justice
for Sam.

195
00:09:50,933 --> 00:09:53,667
The team wants to hold
the Zafras accountable.

196
00:09:53,667 --> 00:09:56,733
We're able to go through
the files Sam was handling

197
00:09:56,733 --> 00:09:58,667
when she was still alive.

198
00:09:58,667 --> 00:10:00,300
So Team Alpha is asking

199
00:10:00,967 --> 00:10:03,300
if this can be
our official case.

200
00:10:06,467 --> 00:10:08,433
You'll go against the Zafras.

201
00:10:09,300 --> 00:10:10,267
Yes, sir.

202
00:10:11,300 --> 00:10:14,000
We want them
to pay for their crimes.

203
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,633
Not just for their crimes
in society, but for Sam, too.

204
00:10:16,633 --> 00:10:18,900
Sir, this is personal to us.

205
00:10:18,900 --> 00:10:21,233
I know you're worried
because what happened to Sam

206
00:10:21,233 --> 00:10:22,933
might happen again.

207
00:10:22,933 --> 00:10:24,367
But I can assure you

208
00:10:24,367 --> 00:10:26,367
that we will work our butts off

209
00:10:26,367 --> 00:10:28,867
so that no agent of NCIA
gets hurt again.

210
00:10:28,867 --> 00:10:31,700
And to put an end
to the Zafras' evil schemes.

211
00:10:31,700 --> 00:10:38,633
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

212
00:10:40,100 --> 00:10:42,867
[CASTOR] We know the Zafra case
matters to Sir Delgado.

213
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:48,033
Team Alpha.

214
00:10:48,033 --> 00:10:49,400
- Sir.
- Sir.

215
00:10:49,400 --> 00:10:50,300
Sir.

216
00:10:51,433 --> 00:10:56,400
Sebastian told me
you want to avenge Sam.

217
00:10:56,400 --> 00:10:57,867
I understand
where you're coming from.

218
00:10:57,867 --> 00:11:00,567
Sir, we're not after revenge.

219
00:11:00,567 --> 00:11:02,833
We want to get justice for her.

220
00:11:02,833 --> 00:11:04,000
Yes, sir.

221
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:07,200
We won't stop until
her killers are behind bars.

222
00:11:09,133 --> 00:11:10,633
From this day forward,

223
00:11:10,633 --> 00:11:13,333
this will officially
be your case.

224
00:11:14,600 --> 00:11:16,800
Find the people who killed Sam

225
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:18,633
so we can bring them
to justice.

226
00:11:18,633 --> 00:11:21,433
I only have one request.

227
00:11:21,433 --> 00:11:23,667
Be transparent with me.

228
00:11:23,667 --> 00:11:26,900
Tell me about
every move you make.

229
00:11:26,900 --> 00:11:31,600
Because I don't want to
lose another agent

230
00:11:31,600 --> 00:11:33,867
because of my negligence.

231
00:11:33,867 --> 00:11:36,033
- Understood?
- [IN UNISON] Yes, sir!

232
00:11:36,033 --> 00:11:38,033
[SEBASTIAN]
We won't let you down, sir.

233
00:11:38,033 --> 00:11:39,100
We promise.

234
00:11:39,100 --> 00:11:41,967
We will do our best.
For Sam.

235
00:11:44,167 --> 00:11:49,100
This will be the NCIA's
most personal case.

236
00:11:49,100 --> 00:11:51,633
I'm counting on you,
Team Alpha.

237
00:11:52,833 --> 00:11:54,000
[SAM PANTING]

238
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:55,700
Wait a minute, buddy.

239
00:11:55,700 --> 00:11:57,033
- Wait.
- What?

240
00:11:57,033 --> 00:11:59,800
I think we've made
enough money.

241
00:11:59,800 --> 00:12:00,833
Are you kidding me?

242
00:12:00,833 --> 00:12:03,967
This is not enough
to cover your expenses at home.

243
00:12:03,967 --> 00:12:06,100
Don't give up now.

244
00:12:07,433 --> 00:12:09,333
We need to keep fighting, bud!

245
00:12:09,333 --> 00:12:15,533
I just don't want to win at the
expense of other people losing.

246
00:12:15,567 --> 00:12:19,533
They could've used that
money to buy milk for their baby

247
00:12:19,533 --> 00:12:21,067
or to cover
their other expenses.

248
00:12:21,067 --> 00:12:25,233
I'm going to be honest, buddy,
I should be teaching you.

249
00:12:25,233 --> 00:12:29,167
But I'm the one
who's learning from you instead.

250
00:12:29,167 --> 00:12:31,267
I wouldn't be surprised
if one day

251
00:12:31,267 --> 00:12:33,167
Gabo comes out a changed man.

252
00:12:33,167 --> 00:12:34,733
- [WOMAN 1] Get out!
- [MAN] No!

253
00:12:34,733 --> 00:12:37,000
- I have had it with you!
- Come on!

254
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:38,800
- You're shameless!
- Please, don't do this!

255
00:12:38,800 --> 00:12:41,800
- Take your stuff and leave!
- Come on! That's just gossip!

256
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:43,067
Don't you dare!

257
00:12:43,067 --> 00:12:44,600
- Come on--
- Go!

258
00:12:44,600 --> 00:12:46,167
- You don't want to leave?!
- I'm begging you!

259
00:12:46,167 --> 00:12:48,000
- Alright. How about now?!
- Babe, please!

260
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:49,533
- You still want to stay?!
- Babe!

261
00:12:49,567 --> 00:12:50,667
- Come here!
- Babe!

262
00:12:50,667 --> 00:12:52,133
I've had it with you!
Come here!

263
00:12:52,133 --> 00:12:53,800
- [WOMAN 2] Get him!
- You shameless man!

264
00:12:53,800 --> 00:12:55,733
[WOMAN 3]
That's what you deserve!

265
00:12:55,733 --> 00:12:58,200
[WOMAN 1] If I catch you,
I'll cut your manhood off!

266
00:12:58,200 --> 00:12:59,833
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

267
00:12:59,833 --> 00:13:02,767
Look, bud.
Problem solved.

268
00:13:02,767 --> 00:13:04,200
[SAM] Hey, wait a minute.

269
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:05,233
Are we really
stealing their clothes?

270
00:13:05,233 --> 00:13:08,000
We're not stealing,
we're just picking them up.

271
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:09,733
Let's go before
someone else gets these!

272
00:13:09,733 --> 00:13:12,167
- Gabo could use these!
- Uh--

273
00:13:12,167 --> 00:13:14,300
Rudy! Rudy!

274
00:13:15,067 --> 00:13:16,600
- What's wrong, Elton?
- It's Gabo!

275
00:13:16,600 --> 00:13:19,167
He's fighting those guys again!

276
00:13:19,167 --> 00:13:20,833
What?! We need to help him!

277
00:13:20,833 --> 00:13:22,333
- Come on!
- No! No! No! Stop!

278
00:13:22,367 --> 00:13:25,667
You'll only make things
worse again!

279
00:13:25,667 --> 00:13:27,967
Gabo can't stay away
from trouble.

280
00:13:27,967 --> 00:13:29,900
Well, knowing Gabo,

281
00:13:29,900 --> 00:13:31,567
- he can handle this.
- [MAMENG] Oh, dear.

282
00:13:31,567 --> 00:13:35,167
Mister Rudy,
Gabo will definitely retaliate.

283
00:13:36,833 --> 00:13:40,000
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

284
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:42,700
- Oh, Gloria's here.
- [MAMENG] Move it.

285
00:13:42,700 --> 00:13:43,967
- It's Gloria.
- So?

286
00:13:43,967 --> 00:13:45,533
Did you see Gabo?

287
00:13:45,533 --> 00:13:48,400
- No.
- No? Why are you in a hurry?

288
00:13:48,400 --> 00:13:51,300
We tricked the organizers
of the cockfight.

289
00:13:51,300 --> 00:13:53,033
We were losing.

290
00:13:53,033 --> 00:13:55,467
So I yelled, "Cops!"
and everyone ran!

291
00:13:55,500 --> 00:13:57,767
Then we found some clothes
for Gabo.

292
00:13:57,767 --> 00:14:00,667
- Oh, that's good.
- What's the commotion about?

293
00:14:00,667 --> 00:14:03,300
- Gabo's in trouble again!
- [MAMENG] Yes.

294
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:05,700
[DANTE] The people he fought
last night came back.

295
00:14:05,700 --> 00:14:08,300
What? We need to help him.
Where is he?

296
00:14:08,300 --> 00:14:11,100
- Come on! Follow me!
- Let's go!

297
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:12,867
- Come on.
- Mister Dante.

298
00:14:12,867 --> 00:14:14,067
- Go ahead.
- Oh, dear.

299
00:14:14,067 --> 00:14:21,067
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

300
00:14:26,667 --> 00:14:31,133
[GROANS] Good morning,
one million pesos!

301
00:14:31,167 --> 00:14:32,400
[GIGGLES]

302
00:14:33,267 --> 00:14:40,267
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

303
00:14:54,800 --> 00:15:01,000
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

304
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:03,800
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

305
00:15:03,833 --> 00:15:09,467
[BETCHAY] <i> Who wouldn't want
</i> to wake up to a million pesos?

306
00:15:09,467 --> 00:15:12,667
<i>Money was the first thing
I used to worry about</i>

307
00:15:12,667 --> 00:15:14,933
<i> when I woke up.</i>

308
00:15:14,933 --> 00:15:19,033
<i> Now, my only problem is</i>

309
00:15:19,033 --> 00:15:22,967
<i>whether I'll deposit it
in a bank</i>

310
00:15:22,967 --> 00:15:25,067
<i> or just keep it here.</i>

311
00:15:25,067 --> 00:15:26,433
<i> Like an investment!</i>

312
00:15:27,433 --> 00:15:28,700
<i> Oh, my...</i>

313
00:15:29,600 --> 00:15:32,967
<i>I guess this is the struggle
of the rich:</i>

314
00:15:32,967 --> 00:15:36,200
<i>deciding how
to spend their money.</i>

315
00:15:37,700 --> 00:15:42,500
<i>And now...
it's my struggle too.</i>

316
00:15:42,500 --> 00:15:47,067
<i> Because I'm rich now!</i>

317
00:15:47,067 --> 00:15:54,033
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

318
00:16:04,900 --> 00:16:11,867
[MUSIC TURNS CURIOUS]

319
00:16:14,800 --> 00:16:16,400
Where is everyone?

320
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:23,433
[CURIOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

321
00:16:23,433 --> 00:16:24,633
[HUFFS]

322
00:16:25,400 --> 00:16:26,933
Useless people.

323
00:16:28,033 --> 00:16:29,833
They only have one job.

324
00:16:29,833 --> 00:16:31,933
And yet, they can't even
do it properly.

325
00:16:31,933 --> 00:16:34,733
It's only right that
I expect them to serve me!

326
00:16:34,733 --> 00:16:38,433
Me, the one who feeds them!

327
00:16:38,433 --> 00:16:43,200
Me, the one who works herself
to the bone to pay the bills!

328
00:16:43,833 --> 00:16:46,933
It's kind of pathetic
when someone can't hustle.

329
00:16:46,933 --> 00:16:49,467
No ambitions, no dreams.

330
00:16:49,467 --> 00:16:50,867
Not like me.

331
00:16:50,867 --> 00:16:53,700
A millionaire.

332
00:16:54,633 --> 00:16:57,967
So what if I sold the land?

333
00:16:57,967 --> 00:16:59,000
Is that wrong?

334
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:00,300
My only mistake

335
00:17:00,300 --> 00:17:02,800
is not having done it
years ago.

336
00:17:02,800 --> 00:17:05,267
Anyway, I only have
one message for them.

337
00:17:05,700 --> 00:17:07,633
Boo-hoo!

338
00:17:07,633 --> 00:17:08,800
[INHALES DEEPLY]

339
00:17:08,800 --> 00:17:10,500
I deserved this!
[CHUCKLES]

340
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:13,200
- [GLASS CLINKS, THUDS]
- [SIGHING]

341
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:14,233
[SPOON CLATTERS]

342
00:17:14,233 --> 00:17:17,033
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

343
00:17:17,067 --> 00:17:19,500
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

344
00:17:21,200 --> 00:17:24,133
[BETCHAY]  I deserve to eat
something delicious.

345
00:17:26,200 --> 00:17:28,100
<i> I'll dine out.</i>

346
00:17:29,333 --> 00:17:31,167
<i> Because now I'm rich.</i>

347
00:17:31,967 --> 00:17:32,933
[SCOFFS]

348
00:17:33,567 --> 00:17:34,600
[GLASS THUDS]

349
00:17:34,600 --> 00:17:36,400
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

350
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:37,933
- [EXHALES]
- [CHAIR SCRAPES]

351
00:17:38,500 --> 00:17:39,500
[PLASTIC BAG CRINKLES]

352
00:17:41,400 --> 00:17:42,567
[MONEY RUSTLING]

353
00:17:42,567 --> 00:17:43,600
[GIGGLES]

354
00:17:48,533 --> 00:17:51,200
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING]

355
00:17:51,867 --> 00:17:55,833
So this is what it feels like
to have one million pesos.

356
00:17:55,833 --> 00:17:58,067
You've already counted it...
[INHALES DEEPLY]

357
00:17:58,067 --> 00:18:01,067
...but you still want
to count it again.

358
00:18:01,067 --> 00:18:02,500
I know what I'm going to do.

359
00:18:02,500 --> 00:18:04,267
[CLEARS THROAT, INHALES]

360
00:18:04,267 --> 00:18:07,567
I'm going to do it
just like in the movies.

361
00:18:08,333 --> 00:18:15,333
- [IMITATES WIND WHOOSHING]
- [MONEY FLAPPING]

362
00:18:15,333 --> 00:18:18,833
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

363
00:18:18,833 --> 00:18:25,800
[WHOOPING, GIGGLING]

364
00:18:25,833 --> 00:18:27,333
[BREATHING EXCITEDLY]

365
00:18:27,333 --> 00:18:29,167
It feels so good!

366
00:18:29,167 --> 00:18:30,800
Oh, the scent!

367
00:18:30,800 --> 00:18:34,667
[WHOOPING, GIGGLING]

368
00:18:34,667 --> 00:18:36,533
This is the dream!

369
00:18:37,367 --> 00:18:40,833
[GIGGLING]

370
00:18:40,833 --> 00:18:43,567
This must be the feeling
of true peace of mind!

371
00:18:43,567 --> 00:18:47,900
[CHUCKLING]

372
00:18:47,900 --> 00:18:50,900
So good! It's pure bliss!

373
00:18:50,900 --> 00:18:54,033
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

374
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:57,767
[OVERLAPPING CLAMOR]

375
00:18:57,833 --> 00:19:02,633
[GUNSHOTS]

376
00:19:02,633 --> 00:19:03,700
[TEKLA] Let's go!

377
00:19:05,133 --> 00:19:06,433
[GABO GRUNTS]

378
00:19:08,100 --> 00:19:09,333
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [MAN GRUNTS]

379
00:19:09,333 --> 00:19:10,600
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

380
00:19:11,300 --> 00:19:12,367
[BLOW LANDS]

381
00:19:12,533 --> 00:19:13,667
[SLINGSHOT SNAPS]

382
00:19:13,667 --> 00:19:14,767
[BLOW LANDS]

383
00:19:18,033 --> 00:19:20,700
- [SLINGSHOT SNAPS]
- [MEN GRUNTING]

384
00:19:21,067 --> 00:19:22,367
